    "composition_notes": "Three voices only: a bright_lead for the mock-heroic descending lament, a plodding root-fifth bass for heavy-footed comedy, and sparse noise thuds that land on downbeats and stop dead before the phrase resolves. A minor with a borrowed G# leading tone and a stepwise B-section climb that peaks too high and collapses. Wide gaps, untidy rests and a two-step silence before every pickup are the comic timing; the bass drops out of the harmony notes so the last tonic thud can stand alone."
